' 4+1 development view - Development view · from the controller to the front end types
' Version 1.1 - 2026-11-10
' For: whoever is going to change the code.
' Documented decision: The API types in the front end are generated from OpenAPI, never written by hand, and CI checks for drift.
' Not drawn: classes, endpoints and business rules.
@startuml development-api-types
!include ../style.puml
title Development view - from the controller to the front end types

start
:Change a controller or a DTO\n(Api, Application);
:dotnet build backend/SportsBooking.slnx\nMicrosoft.Extensions.ApiDescription.Server\ngenerates the OpenAPI document;
note right
  The generator starts the application as GetDocument.Insider
  and Program.cs gives it placeholder settings.
end note
:OpenAPI document\nbackend/src/SportsBooking.Api/openapi/sportsbooking-api.json;
:cd frontend && npm run gen:api\nopenapi-typescript 7.13.0;
:Generated API types\nfrontend/src/lib/api/schema.d.ts;
:The modules in features/ and lib/ use\nimport type { components } from "@/lib/api/schema";
:Commit both generated files;
if (CI: would the document or the types change?) then (yes)
  :CI fails: git diff ~-~-exit-code;
  stop
else (no)
  :CI green;
  stop
endif

@enduml
